          },
          "code": "GENERATE_INITIAL_INFO_DISPLAYS",
          "id": "1765167572073",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765167572074_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Input:\n  {{$context.$nodes.RESTRICT_THE_ACCOUNTS.$output}}\n\n  The input contains rows with:\n  ownedProductName, ownedProductId, accounts, potentialRevenueAmount, industries.\n\n  Generate exactly:\n  1. One oraInfoDisplay with patternId \"multiRecordWidget\".\n  2. Up to two low-priority oraInsight blocks after the oraInfoDisplay.\n\n  Do not output any text before, between, or after these blocks.\n\n  oraInfoDisplay requirements:\n  - key: \"list\"\n  - patternId: \"multiRecordWidget\"\n  - title: \"{TOTAL_ACCOUNTS} out of total {{$context.$nodes.TOTAL_TARGETABLE_ACCOUNTS.$output.result}} accounts have a good fit for {{$context.$variables.targetProductName}}.\"\n  - description: exactly two short paragraphs in the same JSON description field, separated by \"\\n\\n\".\n  - properties.cols must be exactly:\n    [\"Existing Product\", \"Accounts\", \"Potential Revenue\", \"Top Industries\"]\n\n  Description requirements:\n  Generate exactly two short paragraphs in the same JSON description field, separated by \"\\n\\n\".\n\n  Paragraph 1:\n  Write an executive summary explaining that these accounts were selected based on strong Product Fit, existing installed-product ownership, and\n  established Buying Group availability. State that the top three installed-product segments represent the strongest adoption opportunity for\n  {{$context.$variables.targetProductName}} because they combine adoption likelihood, potential revenue, and cross-sell relevance.\n\n  Paragraph 2:\n  Write a sales and marketing insight explaining why customers in these top three installed-product segments are strong candidates for\n  {{$context.$variables.targetProductName}}. Position {{$context.$variables.targetProductName}} as a natural extension of existing customer\n  investments, with messaging focused on productivity, visibility, operational agility, and measurable business impact.\n\n  Style constraints:\n  - Use executive, specific, business-ready language.\n  - Avoid generic marketing phrases such as \"robust cloud solutions\", \"drive efficiency and innovation\", or \"seamlessly extend capabilities\".\n  - Do not mention raw field names, technical identifiers, or internal scoring logic.\n  - Do not output either paragraph outside the description field.\n\n  Row mapping:\n  - \"Existing Product\": ownedProductName\n  - \"Accounts\": accounts\n  - \"Potential Revenue\": format potentialRevenueAmount:\n    - if potentialRevenueAmount >= 1000000000, use two decimals with \"B\"\n    - otherwise use two decimals with \"M\"\n  - \"Top Industries\": unique industries joined by \", \"; drop null, empty, and duplicate values\n\n  Sorting and summary logic:\n  - Sort rows by potentialRevenueAmount descending.\n  - Use the top 3 rows after sorting for the table.\n  - TOTAL_ACCOUNTS = sum of accounts across the top 3 rows, or fewer if fewer than 3 rows exist.\n\n  oraInsight requirements:\n  Generate low-priority oraInsight blocks for the first 2 rows after sorting only.\n\n  Each oraInsight must use:\n  - title: \"Show Insights for <Existing Product>\"\n  - shortDescription: one focused sentence about the cross-sell value for that installed-product segment\n  - actionText: \"Show Insights\"\n  - priority: false\n  - followUpCommand: \"ora.Invoke(\\\"showInsights\\\", \\\"showInsights({\\\"targetProductId\\\":\\\"{{$context.$variables.targetProductId}}\\\",\n  \\\"ownedProductId\\\":\\\"<ownedProductId>\\\",\\\"ownedProductName\\\":\\\"<ownedProductName>\\\"})\\\")\"\n\n  Replacement rules:\n  - <Existing Product> = ownedProductName\n  - <ownedProductId> = ownedProductId\n  - <ownedProductName> = ownedProductName\n  - targetProductId must always be {{$context.$variables.targetProductId}}\n\n  Hard constraints:\n  - Output only the oraInfoDisplay and oraInsight blocks.\n  - Do not output explanatory text, markdown, headings, or commentary outside the blocks.\n  - The executive summary and sales-marketing insight must appear only inside the multiRecordWidget description field.\n  - The description must contain exactly two paragraphs and no bullets.\n  - Do not create more than two oraInsight blocks.\n  - Do not output null. Use an empty string for missing values."
            },
            {
              "id": "1765167572073_systemPrompt",
